  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "The fashion and costumes also bridged the gap between pop performance and rave culture, with groups like Caramell utilizing spiked, dyed hair and UV-reactive neon textiles that mirrored the style of club kids. Costuming was rarely casual; it leaned into theatrical roleplay, with Me & My’s latex cat-suits exemplifying a campy, costume-party approach to sexuality that remained playful rather than explicitly erotic."
  },
